// Markdown rules that catch a rendering bug, not a style preference.
//
// Deliberately small. Running the default set over this repo reports
// 1127 findings, nearly all of them cosmetic or wrong: MD013 would
// flag AGENTS.md, whose lines are long on purpose; MD038 flags
// `question [Y/n]: ` and `- `, where the trailing space is the thing
// being documented; MD018 reads prose starting "#8 ..." as a broken
// heading. A linter that is wrong more often than right gets ignored,
// which is the state `make clippy` avoids by being -D warnings.
//
// Add a rule here once the repo passes it, not before.
{
  "config": {
    "default": false,
    // A fence not surrounded by blank lines can swallow the block
    // after it.
    "MD031": true,
    // A file without a trailing newline concatenates with the next
    // one in tooling that joins them.
    "MD047": true
  },
  "globs": ["**/*.md", "!scratch", "!target"]
}
